# Target C-II — corrected uniform strong-branch orbit-capacity gap `0.0077`

**Date:** 2026-09-15  
**Status:** proof-only matched all-train/rhombic strengthening  
**Scope:** identical to the hostile-audited `g=0.0076` theorem  
**LEVEL I STATUS:** `STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.`

The hostile-audited corrected uniform strong-branch theorem proves the matched atomic
floor

\[
2\sqrt{\Delta_2}+0.0076,
\qquad
\Delta_2={\pi\over2\sqrt3},
\]

by splitting the physical three-phase capacity into three scope-correct branches:

1. a strong `1/10` pair-deficit branch below the explicit strong/fallback threshold;
2. the unconditional `2/29` fallback while the center mass remains at most
   `K=2/sqrt(3)`;
3. a high-center `C>K` branch using only generic triangle-free capacity.

The same analytic proof has enough exact margin to support the stronger safe round
value

\[
\boxed{g=0.0077.}
\]

Put

\[
C_{77}:=2\sqrt{\Delta_2}+0.0077.
\]

Then, at the same proof-only scope,

\[
\boxed{
\liminf {T-q/2\over D}\ge C_{77},
}
\tag{G77.1}

and independently on the strict-rhombus train graph,

\[
\boxed{
\liminf {T_R\over D}\ge C_{77},
\qquad
\liminf {\sigma_R\over D}\ge0.0154.
}
\tag{G77.2}

---

## 1. No change in branch logic

Let `W` be one exact three-phase orbit mass, with ordered phase masses

\[
C\ge U\ge V\ge0,
\qquad W=C+U+V.
\]

Write

\[
K={2\over\sqrt3},
\qquad
r_{crit}=\sqrt{20/29}.
\]

The hostile-audited proof uses exactly the following three branches.

### Strong branch

When the center/leaf excess ratios lie below `r_crit`, the iterative-pruning theorem
supplies the physical missing-pair floor

\[
\rho\ge {1\over10}(a+b-K)_+^2.
\]

The resulting physical one-orbit capacity is `Psi_s(W)`.

### Fallback branch

Past the strong threshold but still with `C<=K`, use only the unconditional physical
pair theorem

\[
\rho\ge {2\over29}(a+b-K)_+^2.
\]

The fallback capacity is `B_0(W)`.

### High-center branch

For `C>K`, no physical pair theorem is invoked.  Use only

\[
E\le C(W-C),
\]

which is maximized at `C=K` because the relevant orbit interval lies below `2K`.

Thus the `0.0077` strengthening inherits the exact scope repair already hostile-audited
at `0.0076`; it does not extend either physical pair theorem beyond its hypotheses.

---

## 2. Exact certificate

The verifier

`research/verify_target_c_uniform_strong_branch_orbit_capacity_gap_0077.py`

uses exact `Fraction` arithmetic, Machin bounds for `pi`, and integer-square-root
enclosures for every radical.  It reproduces every load-bearing derivative and branch
comparison from the `0.0076` certificate with

\[
A_0=C_{77}.
\]

The exact outward bounds include

\[
A_0<1.912325614,
\qquad
M_0={4\Delta_2\over A_0}>1.896956617,
\]

and the worst center/leaf excess ratio in the strong half-orbit interval satisfies

\[
0.79236<\sqrt{20/29}=0.83045\ldots .
\]

The dominant-mass total-capacity derivative remains strictly positive:

\[
\boxed{Q_s'(W)>0.59668.}
\tag{G77.3}

The exact endpoint branch margins are

\[
\boxed{
\Delta_2-\Psi_s(C_{77})
>6.67\times10^{-6},
}
\tag{G77.4}

\[
\boxed{
\Delta_2-B_0(C_{77})
>1.394\times10^{-3},
}
\tag{G77.5}

and

\[
\boxed{
\Delta_2-B_H(C_{77})
>3.206\times10^{-2}.
}
\tag{G77.6}

For the strong tangent certificate the verifier uses

\[
c_0=0.935386
\]

and the strong concavity `Phi_CC<=-2`.  The outward bound on the tangent error is
small enough that the residual strong margin remains above `6.6e-6`.

Thus total exact atomic mass at most `C77` cannot carry the required strict-rhombus
crossing density `Delta2`.  The same exposed-hull transfer used in the audited parent
then gives (G77.1), and the rhombic-only copy gives (G77.2).

---

## 3. Numerical ceiling is not used

A non-load-bearing floating-point solve puts the strong capacity zero near

\[
g=0.00770727\ldots .
\]

The proof does **not** claim that value.  At `g=0.0077` the exact strong margin is only
about `6.67e-6`, so there is little useful room left in this architecture.  Further
progress should use a new structural constraint rather than another un-audited decimal
push.

---

## 4. Downstream substitution

The safe matched replacement is now

```text
C_77 = 2 sqrt(Delta_2) + 0.0077,
(T-q/2)/D >= C_77 - o(1),
T_R/D       >= C_77 - o(1),
sigma_R/D   >= 0.0154 - o(1).
```

The restored-incidence and residual-stability arguments can use `C77` in place of
`C76`.  Because the exact strong endpoint margin is much smaller than at `g=.0076`, a
residual-stability proof should retain the derivative information rather than spend the
endpoint margin twice.

**Disposition:** proved proof-only matched atomic strengthening; C-II and Level I remain open.
